  "confidence": 0.98,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["U9", "U1", "U4", "U6"],
      "pins": ["U9.1", "U9.2", "U9.4", "U1.6", "U4.2", "U6.5"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U9-Pad1)", "Net-(U9-Pad2)", "Net-(U9-Pad4)"],
      "observed": "An unlisted 74LVC1G86 XOR gate takes ESP32 GPIO3 and thermocouple channel 3's T- input as its inputs, then drives the TPS1H200 heater switch's DELAY pin. The T- signal is therefore also connected to digital logic, and the switch delay control is driven by the XOR output.",
      "expected": "The specification describes the thermocouple pair as wiring directly to the MAX31855 differential inputs and describes the heater switch without a digital logic path from a thermocouple input or GPIO3 to DELAY. The extra gate and these connections should not be present; the switch delay pin should be configured appropriately for its intended function.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U9\") (value \"74LVC1G86\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"34\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"GPIO3/ADC1_CH3\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"35\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad2)\") (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"T-\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"36\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad4)\") (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"DELAY\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"4\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Thermocouple wire pair connects to a 2-pin screw terminal ... whose two pins wire directly to the MAX31855's differential thermocouple inputs T+ (pin 3) and T- (pin 2)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The thermocouple input can influence the heater switch's delay behavior through the XOR gate. Since a thermocouple signal is small and the gate input is not described as biased or conditioned, its logic state may be indeterminate or noise-sensitive; this can make switch fault timing unpredictable and may disturb temperature sensing.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist contains an undocumented XOR gate connecting a thermocouple input and ESP32 GPIO3 to the heater switch's DELAY pin. This creates an unintended signal path that can make the switch's delay behavior unpredictable."
}

